---
import MainLayout from '@/layouts/MainLayout.astro';
import LegalFooter from '@/components/LegalFooter.astro';
import { PAGE_DESCRIPTIONS } from '@/lib/seo/defaults';
import { CONSENT_COOKIE_NAME, CONSENT_MAX_AGE_SECONDS, CONSENT_VERSION } from '@/lib/consent/config';
import '@/styles/legal-pages.css';

const consentDays = Math.round(CONSENT_MAX_AGE_SECONDS / (24 * 60 * 60));
---

<MainLayout
  title="Cookie Policy | Kersivo"
  description={PAGE_DESCRIPTIONS.cookies}
  canonicalPath="/cookies"
>
  <main class="legal-page">
    <article class="container legal-page__inner">
      <h1 class="legal-page__title">Cookie Policy</h1>
      <p class="legal-page__updated">Last updated: 31 July 2026</p>

      <p>
        This Cookie Policy explains how KERSIVO uses cookies and similar technologies on
        <a href="https://kersivo.co.uk/">kersivo.co.uk</a>. It should be read with our
        <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>. Rejecting optional technologies does not block necessary services such as
        browsing, booking demos, contact forms or paying for a monthly subscription. Mentions of a setup deposit below
        refer to a gated legacy checkout path that is not currently offered publicly.
      </p>

      <h2>What are cookies and similar technologies?</h2>
      <p>
        Cookies are small text files stored on your device. Similar technologies include localStorage, sessionStorage
        and tags/scripts that set identifiers. Some are necessary for the site to work. Others help us understand usage
        or measure advertising, and are used only with your permission.
      </p>

      <h2>How we ask for consent</h2>
      <p>
        On your first visit (and again when our consent version changes), we show a banner with comparable actions to
        accept all optional technologies, reject optional technologies, or manage preferences. Your choice is stored in
        a first-party necessary cookie (<code>{CONSENT_COOKIE_NAME}</code>, consent version {CONSENT_VERSION}, about{' '}
        {consentDays} days). You can reopen preferences at any time via <strong>Cookie settings</strong> in the footer.
      </p>
      <p>
        We use Google Consent Mode v2 with a privacy-first approach: analytics and advertising tags are not loaded until
        you grant the relevant permission. <code>ad_personalization</code> is granted only if you switch on personalised
        advertising, and remains denied for every other combination of choices.
      </p>

      <h2>Categories we use</h2>
      <h3>Necessary</h3>
      <p>
        Required for security, payments, forms, booking functionality, remembering your privacy choices, and keeping a
        barbershop admin signed in so you can manage your workspace securely without logging in on every visit. When a
        valid admin session cookie is present, opening the Admin &amp; Shop product preview takes you straight to your
        signed-in workspace (without signing in with Google again). These cannot be switched off through the preference
        tool.
      </p>
      <h3>Analytics</h3>
      <p>
        Off by default. When accepted, Google Analytics 4 helps us understand how visitors use the site. Provider:
        Google.
      </p>
      <h3>Advertising measurement</h3>
      <p>
        Off by default. When accepted and a Google Ads measurement ID is configured, Google Ads tags help us understand
        whether ads lead to enquiries or subscriptions. This category measures results only; on its own it does not add
        you to advertising audiences. We do not use Google Ads Enhanced Conversions.
      </p>
      <h3>Personalised advertising</h3>
      <p>
        Off by default and asked for separately from measurement. When accepted, Google may add you to our remarketing
        audiences so that we can show KERSIVO ads to people who have already visited this site. Provider: Google Ads.
        Switching this off stops future audience collection; audiences you were already added to are managed by Google
        and expire according to their membership duration.
      </p>

      <h2>Technology inventory</h2>
      <p>
        The table below lists technologies we have verified in the KERSIVO application. Google cookie durations can vary
        by Google product configuration; where we cannot verify an exact TTL from our code alone, duration is marked as
        unresolved pending browser verification after consent.
      </p>

      <div class="legal-page__table-wrap">
        <table class="legal-page__table">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th scope="col">Name</th>
              <th scope="col">Provider</th>
              <th scope="col">Category</th>
              <th scope="col">Purpose</th>
              <th scope="col">Duration</th>
              <th scope="col">Party</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td><code>{CONSENT_COOKIE_NAME}</code></td>
              <td>KERSIVO</td>
              <td>Necessary</td>
              <td>Stores your cookie preference version and choices</td>
              <td>{consentDays} days</td>
              <td>First-party cookie</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><code>kersivo_admin_session</code></td>
              <td>KERSIVO</td>
              <td>Necessary</td>
              <td>Keeps an authenticated barbershop admin signed in to the admin panel</td>
              <td>30 days</td>
              <td>First-party cookie</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>
                <code>better-auth.session_token</code> (on HTTPS:
                <code>__Secure-better-auth.session_token</code>)
              </td>
              <td>KERSIVO</td>
              <td>Necessary</td>
              <td>Primary admin authentication session; keeps you signed in to the admin panel and opens your workspace from the Admin &amp; Shop preview when the cookie is valid</td>
              <td>Up to 30 days</td>
              <td>First-party cookie</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><code>kersivo_shop_cart_v2</code></td>
              <td>KERSIVO</td>
              <td>Necessary</td>
              <td>Retail demo basket contents</td>
              <td>Until cleared / localStorage</td>
              <td>First-party localStorage</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><code>kersivo.admin.secret</code></td>
              <td>KERSIVO</td>
              <td>Necessary</td>
              <td>Admin demo authentication helper</td>
              <td>Until cleared / localStorage</td>
              <td>First-party localStorage</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><code>feature261-reports-widget-v1</code></td>
              <td>KERSIVO</td>
              <td>Necessary</td>
              <td>Landing demo reports widget display preferences</td>
              <td>Session</td>
              <td>First-party sessionStorage</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><code>setup_deposit_paid:*</code></td>
              <td>KERSIVO</td>
              <td>Analytics (when consented)</td>
              <td>Prevents duplicate setup deposit conversion events on refresh</td>
              <td>Session</td>
              <td>First-party sessionStorage</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><code>_ga</code>, <code>_ga_*</code>, <code>_gid</code></td>
              <td>Google Analytics</td>
              <td>Analytics (when consented)</td>
              <td>Distinguish visitors / sessions for GA4</td>
              <td>Unresolved — verify in browser after consent</td>
              <td>First-party cookies set via Google</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><code>_gcl_*</code> / Ads cookies (if Ads ID configured)</td>
              <td>Google Ads</td>
              <td>Advertising measurement and/or personalised advertising (when consented)</td>
              <td>Measure ad-driven conversions and, with personalised advertising, build remarketing audiences</td>
              <td>Unresolved — verify in browser after consent</td>
              <td>First-party cookies set via Google</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>URL parameters (<code>gclid</code>, <code>gbraid</code>, <code>wbraid</code>, UTMs)</td>
              <td>KERSIVO / advertising platforms</td>
              <td>See Privacy Policy</td>
              <td>
                May remain in the URL. Passed to Stripe metadata only when you voluntarily start setup checkout — not
                stored in cookies/localStorage before advertising-measurement consent
              </td>
              <td>URL lifetime / Stripe metadata retention</td>
              <td>Not a browser cookie</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <h2>Changing or withdrawing consent</h2>
      <p>
        Use <strong>Cookie settings</strong> in the footer. If you withdraw analytics or advertising measurement, we
        update Google Consent Mode immediately, stop loading optional tags on later visits, and delete removable
        first-party optional cookies and related sessionStorage keys where technically possible. Cookies set on other
        domains by third parties cannot always be deleted from our site; those tags will not be loaded again after
        withdrawal.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions: <a href="mailto:hello@kersivo.co.uk">hello@kersivo.co.uk</a>. Complaints may be made to the
        <a href="https://ico.org.uk/">ICO</a>.
      </p>
    </article>
  </main>
  <LegalFooter />
</MainLayout>
